Requirement-Analysis
ComicCraft – AI Comic Story Creator using Gemini Models
Requirement Analysis
1. Project Overview
ComicCraft is an AI-powered application designed to help users create comics from simple text prompts. The system uses Google Gemini models to generate story ideas, characters, scenes, dialogues, and panel descriptions. The generated content is organized into a comic format that users can review, edit, and export.
The main goal is to reduce the effort required to create a comic while allowing users to retain creative control over the final story.
________________________________________
2. Problem Statement
Creating a comic traditionally requires several skills, including:
•	Story writing
•	Character development
•	Dialogue writing
•	Scene planning
•	Panel composition
•	Illustration
•	Editing
For beginners, combining all these tasks can be time-consuming and difficult.
ComicCraft addresses this problem by providing an AI-assisted workflow where users can provide a basic concept and receive a structured comic that they can further customize.
________________________________________
3. Objectives
The major objectives of ComicCraft are:
1.	To generate comic stories from simple user prompts.
2.	To use Gemini models for intelligent story and dialogue generation.
3.	To automatically create characters and scene descriptions.
4.	To divide stories into suitable comic panels.
5.	To allow users to edit AI-generated content.
6.	To maintain consistency between characters and scenes.
7.	To provide an easy-to-use comic creation interface.
8.	To allow users to save and export their completed comics.
________________________________________
4. Functional Requirements
4.1 User Management
The system should allow users to:
•	Create an account.
•	Log in and log out.
•	Manage their profile.
•	Access previously created comic projects.
4.2 Comic Project Creation
Users should be able to:
•	Create a new comic project.
•	Enter a story idea or prompt.
•	Provide a title.
•	Select a genre.
•	Select a preferred tone or mood.
•	Specify the approximate number of panels/pages.
Example:
Prompt: “A young inventor builds a robot that becomes his best friend.”
________________________________________
4.3 AI Story Generation
The system should use Gemini to:
•	Expand the user's initial idea.
•	Generate a complete storyline.
•	Create a beginning, middle, and ending.
•	Generate plot events.
•	Suggest conflicts and resolutions.
•	Generate alternative story directions when requested.
________________________________________
4.4 Character Generation
ComicCraft should generate character information such as:
•	Character name
•	Age
•	Personality
•	Role in the story
•	Appearance
•	Background
•	Relationships with other characters
Users should also be able to manually edit character details.
________________________________________
4.5 Scene and Panel Generation
The system should divide the story into scenes and panels.
Each panel can contain:
•	Panel number
•	Scene description
•	Character actions
•	Background/environment
•	Dialogue
•	Narration
•	Sound effects
•	Visual-generation prompt
Example:
Panel	Description	Dialogue
1	The inventor works late in his garage.	“Just one more adjustment…”
2	The robot suddenly activates.	“Hello, friend.”
3	The inventor looks shocked.	“You can talk?”
________________________________________
4.6 Dialogue Generation
Gemini should generate dialogue appropriate to:
•	Character personality
•	Scene context
•	Story genre
•	Emotional situation
Users should be able to regenerate or manually modify dialogue.
________________________________________
4.7 Image/Artwork Generation
The system should generate visual prompts from panel descriptions and, where an appropriate image-generation service is integrated, use those prompts to create panel artwork.
The system should support:
•	Character appearance descriptions
•	Scene backgrounds
•	Camera/view descriptions
•	Lighting and mood
•	Comic-art style instructions
________________________________________
4.8 Comic Editor
Users should be able to:
•	Edit story text.
•	Modify characters.
•	Change dialogue.
•	Regenerate individual panels.
•	Rearrange panels.
•	Add or remove panels.
•	Modify captions and speech bubbles.
•	Preview the final comic.
________________________________________
4.9 Save and Export
The system should allow users to:
•	Save projects.
•	Continue editing later.
•	Preview the completed comic.
•	Export the comic as an appropriate document/image format such as PDF.
________________________________________
5. Non-Functional Requirements
Performance
•	AI-generated responses should be returned within a reasonable time.
•	The interface should remain responsive during generation.
•	Large comic projects should be handled efficiently.
Usability
•	The application should have a simple and intuitive interface.
•	Users should not need technical knowledge to create comics.
•	Important actions should be clearly visible.
Reliability
•	The system should handle Gemini/API failures gracefully.
•	User projects should not be lost if an AI generation request fails.
•	Generated content should be saved safely.
Security
•	User authentication data must be protected.
•	API keys must not be exposed in the frontend.
•	Users should only be able to access their own projects.
•	Appropriate input validation should be implemented.
Scalability
The architecture should allow additional users, genres, comic styles, and AI capabilities to be added later without major redesign.
Maintainability
•	The application should use modular components.
•	AI functionality should be separated from the user interface.
•	API interactions should be organized into reusable services.
________________________________________
6. Hardware Requirements
For a cloud-based implementation, the user's device does not need high-end hardware.
Minimum
•	Dual-core processor
•	4 GB RAM
•	5 GB available storage
•	Stable internet connection
•	Modern web browser
Recommended
•	Quad-core processor or better
•	8 GB+ RAM
•	10 GB+ available storage
•	Stable broadband connection
________________________________________
7. Software Requirements
A possible technology stack is:
Component	Technology
Frontend	React / Next.js
Backend	Node.js / Python
AI	Google Gemini API
Database	Firebase / PostgreSQL / MongoDB
Authentication	Firebase Authentication / equivalent
Image generation	Compatible image-generation API
Styling	Tailwind CSS / CSS
Hosting	Cloud-based deployment
Version Control	Git / GitHub
The exact stack can be changed according to the project's implementation requirements.
________________________________________
8. Input Requirements
ComicCraft may accept:
•	Story prompt
•	Comic title
•	Genre
•	Number of panels
•	Character information
•	Art/style preferences
•	Tone or mood
•	Language
•	User modifications
Example:
Title: The Last Robot
Genre: Science Fiction
Tone: Emotional
Panels: 8

Prompt:
"A teenager discovers an abandoned robot in a futuristic city
and tries to repair it."
